# Band setup fed to the REPL on startup by demo/jam/start.sh.
# Edit freely — this is your jam template. The transport is left stopped:
# type `transport start` when you are ready.
key C major
chord out out0:4
style load pop
# All 8 style parts routed to distinct channels so the enriched styles
# (pad/perc/chord2/arp) sound. Percussion shares the GM drum channel (10).
style route drums out0:10
style route perc out0:10
style route bass out0:2
style route chord1 out0:3
style route chord2 out0:7
style route pad out0:5
style route arp out0:6
# Optional backing chord loop -- a chord SEQUENCER, separate from the style.
# Left OFF so the style follows YOUR live chords and holds until you change
# them (pure live arranging). Uncomment for a C-A-F-G backing loop, but note:
# while it plays it drives the chord every bar and, under the current
# arbitration, overrides a chord you press live. Live-transpose over a running
# loop is a deferred feature.
# seq new verse
# seq add C 1bar
# seq add A 1bar
# seq add F 1bar
# seq add G 1bar
# seq loop on
# seq play
transport tempo 96
